    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen diagnostics are changed, the [builtin `nvim.diagnostic.status` DiagnosticChanged autocommand](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/1f4335fe72717e3f4fe3e353fa70f26713f12312/runtime/lua/vim/diagnostic.lua#L1148-L1154) will fire, which will redraw the statusline. If the ui2 pager is open when this happens, this will cause the pager's statusline to display the statusline of the buffer whose diagnostics changed instead of its own.\n\n<img width=\"865\" height=\"561\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/39315380-1a3f-4fbe-96d2-944562969170\" />\n\n(Note: this is `hl-StatusLineNC` displaying while `laststatus=3`)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`minimal.lua`:\n```lua\nrequire('vim._core.ui2').enable()\nvim.o.laststatus = 3\nvim.defer_fn(function()\n  local ns = vim.api.nvim_create_namespace('repo')\n  vim.diagnostic.set(ns, 1, { { lnum = 0, message = 'random error' } }, {})\nend, 1000)\nvim.print('message')\nvim.cmd.mes()\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt doesn't do that.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1202+g1f4335fe72",
